        "original_id": "bf9c8fe1-7213-52fc-92c8-fedde3f5578f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sarah Jacobson, Arthur Hiller, John Fusco\n- Films: I Was a Teenage Serial Killer, The Babe\n- Places: Norwalk, Connecticut; New York City; United States\n- Roles: independent filmmaker, director, writer, producer\n\nFacts:\n- Sarah Jacobson was born on August 25, 1971, in Norwalk, Connecticut.\n- Arthur Hiller was born on November 22, 1923.\n- Sarah Jacobson was an independent filmmaker who wrote, produced, and filmed her own movies.\n- Arthur Hiller was a Canadian-American television and film director who directed over 33 films during a 50-year career.\n- Sarah Jacobson wrote and directed the underground no-budget film I Was a Teenage Serial Killer.\n- The Babe was directed by Arthur Hiller and written by John Fusco.\n- The Babe was released in the United States on April 17, 1992.\n- Sarah Jacobson died in New York City on February 13, 2004.\n- Arthur Hiller died on August 17, 2016.",
